HTML TABLES: Many files have HTML <table> tags. To read them:
python3 -c "import re; [print(' | '.join(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>','',c).strip() for c in re.findall(r'<t[hd][^>]*>(.*?)</t[hd]>',r,re.DOTALL))) for t in re.findall(r'<table>(.*?)</table>',open('/app/resources/FILENAME').read(),re.DOTALL) for r in re.findall(r'<tr>(.*?)</tr>',t,re.DOTALL)]"
When columns show "Dept > Sub-category", sum all sub-columns for the department total.

FORMAT: Numeric answer only in answer.txt. Arrays: '[val1, val2]'.

VERIFY: Re-read the exact cell. If multiple matches, check headers match the question.
If wrong, overwrite. Never delete answer.txt.

